<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ's Carter gets whip back for National.</title>
<headline>NZ's Carter gets whip back for National.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>John Carter has been reappointed the National Party's whip, Radio New Zealand reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>Carter lost the job after he was exposed for pretending to be a Maori beneficiary on fellow MP John Bank's talkback radio show.</p>
<p>Roger Sowry, the former whip, has been appointed Minister of Social Welfare.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
